ve, I need to collect.\n\nBetter: Let me find the emerging item's slot. When the mushroom emerges, it's an object. The enemy arrays $000F-$0014 (active), $0016-$001B (type), $006E-$0073 (page), $0087-$008C (x), $00CF-$00D4 (y). The mushroom will occupy a slot with some type. Let me observe: hit the block, then read the arrays; the slot with a new active flag and a type value = the powerup. That type value would be the \"item type\" (e.g. 0/1/2...). Then write 2 to it (or whatever star value) before it emerges.\n\nBut the task says \"changing it before the item comes out\". If I change the type right after the block is hit but while the item is still emerging, it might work (the item's graphics/behavior read the type each frame?) or might not (the type is used at spawn to set up).\n\nHmm. Let me think about SMB's powerup code: The block bump spawns the powerup with its type, and the powerup's \"type\" determines its sprite and behavior. In SMB the powerup is an \"enemy object\" with ID $2E (mushroom?) etc., but the star is ID $2F? Actually, I recall the powerup object IDs: $2E = powerup, and the specific type (mushroom/flower/star/1up) is stored in $0039? Hmm.\n\nActually, from the $0756 mapping: \"CPU $D80C LDA $39 (item type)\". So $0039 holds the item type of the powerup that Mario is touching. That means $0039 is the powerup's live type field. So while the item emerges, $0039 (or the object's type field copied) holds 0/1/2.\n\nBut wait, $0039 is in the \"enemy\" array region? $0039 = 57. Hmm, not in the arrays I know. Actually $0039 might be a dedicated \"powerup type\" variable, only set when a powerup is active.\n\nLet me test: hit the block, then read $0039 over the emergence. If it reads 0 (mushroom), then writing 2 there should turn it into a star.\n\nLet me do it empirically:\n1. Get Mario to the left ? block of the brick row, small.\n2. Save state.\n3. Jump to hit the block.\n4. Read $0039 and the enemy arrays; identify the powerup slot/type.\n\nThe challenge: Mario must be big? The mapping's fire_flower entry says being big changes the mushroom block into a fire flower. So for a star via type change, small Mario hitting the block gives a mushroom (type 0). Then change the type to 2 → star.\n\nLet me first navigate to the ? block. The current state (Koopa) is far a","truncated":true}
