e (mushroom) and another ? block. Actually: bricks: [b][?][b][b][?][b]? and a hidden 1-UP block.\n5. Then the pipes.\n\nHmm.\n\nOur layout data at x=320-448: type7(x=320), type7(x=336), type3(x=352), type7(x=368), type9(x=448). Hmm, and after R5 (x=368), R6 is x=448. So between 368 and 448 there's nothing. Hmm, but there's the lone high ? block at level ~400 (from the screenshot). Hmm, R6 x=448 type 9. Hmm.\n\nHmm, wait, maybe my x computation is off. Let me redo: object x = page*256 + xcol*16? Or x = page*256 + xcol*16? For R3 (xcol 5) page1: 256+80=336. OK.\n\nBut maybe object x = xcol*16 + (byte1 & 0x0F)*? Hmm, the mapping said byte1 low nibble = per-type parameter. Hmm.\n\nOK. Let me just brute-force test ? blocks with teleportation. Actually — simpler: use the block type buffer once I find it.\n\nLet me reconsider the $0647 hit. Let me test whether $0647 holds the block type by reading it and the surrounding region now, and comparing with the left ? block.\n\nActually, here's a cleaner experiment: hit the LEFT ? block (336) and diff $0400-$06FF; then hit the RIGHT ? block (368) and diff. The block-buffer entries will differ in address by (368-336)/16 = 2 blocks. That would confirm the buffer and stride. But that's more experiments.\n\nHmm. Let me instead read $0640-$0650 now (after hit) and also read what it looked like before. I have pre2 snapshot but not the bytes. I can't read snapshots directly.\n\nOK, let me do a targeted experiment: \n- load slot 6 (right ? intact, left ? intact)\n- read $0640-$0660 (record)\n- hit right ? block\n- read $0640-$0660 again\n- find the changed byte(s)\n\nActually the diff already told me: $0647 changed $C0→$23. And $06B7 0→8, $06D4 3→5. Hmm.\n\nLet me now test the LEFT ? block similarly: load slot 5 (Mario at x=295, under the left ? block 336? no — slot 5 was saved at x=295 which is LEFT of the left ? block). Hmm. I need Mario under the left ? block at 344-351... let me just place him via writes.\n\nAlternatively, since both